source-manifest.json records the upstream snapshot and SHA-256 of every
original file and retained runtime header. Adapted headers have one runtime
copy; patches/ records changes against the original hashes.

RTP-LLM adapters are outside this directory. They translate native resource
layouts and launch the original Q FP4, C4 compression, FP4 Norm/RoPE/store,
BF16 Prefill TopK, FP32 Decode TopK and masked SwiGLU/MXFP4 kernels without
importing the SGLang Python package.

compat/sgl_kernel/tensor.h adapts the host-only device-name lookup for the
RTP PPU clang13/GCC10 toolchain, which crashes compiling the ranges projection.
The maximum enumerator is explicit; tensor checks and device arithmetic are
unchanged. The original hash and host adaptation patch are retained in the manifest.
compat/fused_norm_rope_v2.cuh replaces five C++20 using-enum declarations
with equivalent constexpr names for GCC10, including the two host wrappers.
The manifest retains the original hash and the adaptation patch.
compat/topk_prefill_bf16.cuh replaces the host kernel-pointer std::bit_cast
with reinterpret_cast for GCC10; selection and tie handling are unchanged.
compat/topk_decode_v1.cuh makes the same host kernel-pointer conversion for
the FP32 Decode TopK. Selection and tie handling remain unchanged.
compat/c4_decode_v2.cuh skips negative state-write slots used by RTP graph
padding. compat/fused_norm_rope_v2.cuh also skips negative output slots.
Valid rows retain the original arithmetic and cache layout.
